From 098dcf7230267b804ece2a25eb4630e169e94c01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crazynucfan <127292955+crazynucfan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:44:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: apollo_defconfig: nftables fib for the inet family

Podman's netavark sets up container networking with an inet-family
nftables table whose rules use fib expressions; without NFT_FIB_INET the
kernel rejects them ("Could not process rule: No such file or
directory") and no container with a network starts. The other node
kernels (negroni, rhodep) build it as a module; IPv4 and IPv6 fib are
already there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/apollo_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/apollo_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/apollo_defconfig
index a156f4cd5..9ea75bc61 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/apollo_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/apollo_defconfig
@@ -170,6 +170,7 @@ CONFIG_NFT_QUOTA=m
 CONFIG_NFT_REJECT=m
 CONFIG_NFT_COMPAT=m
 CONFIG_NFT_HASH=m
+CONFIG_NFT_FIB_INET=m
 CONFIG_NFT_XFRM=m
 CONFIG_NFT_SOCKET=m
 CONFIG_NFT_OSF=m
-- 
2.53.0

